                <track-text descriptor="document-title" x="438" y="569" alignment="6" visibility="4105" dx="7726" dy="10037" cx="0" cy="0" screen-dx="1020" screen-dy="1330">F-Pn Thibault-IWeiss Ã  Rome</track-text>
                <track-text descriptor="document-author" x="139" y="166" alignment="6" visibility="9" dx="9790" dy="5477" cx="0" cy="0" screen-dx="1020" screen-dy="1330">Peter P.M. Steur (Italy)</track-text>
                <track-text descriptor="document-source" x="185" y="1055" alignment="6" visibility="4105" dx="3263" dy="18609" cx="0" cy="0" screen-dx="1020" screen-dy="1330">F-Pn RÃ©s Vma ms. 1213Olim: Library Mad. ThibaultMany works in this manuscript can be dated after 1740,ie. some 30 years after Weiss' stay in Rome.Thus, it is likely that the frontpage of ms. 1213 was switchedwith that of ms 61, the other Thibault manuscript.</track-text>
                <track-text descriptor="document-transcriber" x="510" y="275" alignment="0" visibility="1" dx="0" dy="0" cx="0" cy="0" screen-dx="1020" screen-dy="1330"/>
